// CoRR -- one thread writes 1 then 2, the other reads 2 and then 1.
//
// WebAssembly memory model: Watt, Rossberg & Pichon-Pharabod, "Weakening
// WebAssembly" (OOPSLA 2019), Fig. 7. Accesses in mode sc are seqcst, every
// other access unordered.
//
// The paper's Fig. 1: unordered accesses need not be coherent, so a racing
// reader may see a writer's stores out of order. Over seqcst accesses
// sc-last-visible forbids it, but that variant tests nothing here: sMRD's
// preserved program order keeps two seqcst reads of one location in order, so
// MoRDor never generates the execution for Wasm to reject.
x := 0;
{
  x.store(1, na);
  x.store(2, na)
} ||| {
  r1 := x.load(na);
  r2 := x.load(na)
}
%%
allow (r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [Wasm]
forbid (r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [SC, RC11]
